5433,1.209892,0.856973,[80,401,61,402],1.201097,0.873121,[404,405,61,406],162.8283,1.183373,0.904,[408,409,61,410],164.9708,1.169358,0.926943,[412,413,61,414],167.1132,1.154899,0.949535,[416,417,61,418],169.2557,1.139938,0.971714,[420,421,61,422],171.3982,1.124523,0.993505,[424,425,61,426],173.5407,1.108686,1.014925,[428,429,61,430],175.6831,1.092359,1.035896,[432,433,61,434],177.8256,1.075619,1.056475,[436,437,61,438],179.9681,1.058474,1.076656,[440,441,61,442],182.1106,1.040867,1.096368,[444,445,61,446],184.253,1.02288,1.115678,[448,449,61,450],186.3955,1.004495,1.134556,[452,453,61,454],188.538,0.985694,1.152962,[456,457,61,458],190.6805,0.966535,1.170951,[460,461,61,462],192.823,0.94699,1.188471,[84,464,61,465],0.926745,1.205792,[467,468,61,469],197.1079,0.906815,1.222136,[471,472,61,473],199.2504,0.886187,1.238248,[92,475,61,476],0.859187,1.258307,[478,479,61,480],203.5353,0.853481,1.262185,[482,479,61,480],205.6778,[484,479,61,480],207.8203,[486,479,61,480],209.9628,[488,479,61,480],212.1053,"Opportunity","ROVER · FLOWN","Held the Mars driving record (45.16 km) until Perseverance passed it in October 2026; 14-year surface lifetime against a 90-sol design","Opportunity drove a marathon across another planet. Spirit’s twin, landed in 2004 for a ninety-day mission, it worked for fourteen years and crossed more than forty-five kilometres — the longest distance any vehicle had travelled on any world until Perseverance passed it in October 2026. It came down, by luck, in a small crater whose walls exposed exactly the water-laid rock it was sent to find, and then it just kept going, crater to crater, reading the ancient water story of Mars mile after mile. A planet-wide dust storm finally silenced it in 2018.","Opportunity (MER-B) hit a planetary jackpot — its airbag-cocooned lander bounced 26 times across Meridiani Planum and rolled into a 22-m crater (Eagle) by sheer luck, surrounded by exposed bedrock a rover could read without driving. First images showed jarosite + \"blueberry\" hematite concretions, the strongest mineral evidence to that point of standing liquid water on early Mars. Over 14 years 138 days (5,111 sols) Opportunity traversed 45.16 km — the Mars rover marathon record, held until Perseverance passed it in October 2026 — visiting Endurance, Victoria, and Endeavour craters. A planet-wide dust storm in June 2018 blocked sunlight from its solar panels; final transmission was 2018-06-10, and NASA declared end-of-mission 2019-02-13.",[495,499,500,503,507,511,516],{"met":61,"label":496,"note":497,"type":498},"LAUNCH","Delta II 7925H Heavy from Cape Canaveral LC-17B.","nominal",{"met":71,"label":73,"note":74,"type":498},{"met":84,"label":501,"note":502,"type":498},"TCM-4","Final pre-EDL trim.",{"met":12,"label":504,"note":505,"type":506},"EDL","Heat shield, parachute, retro-rockets, airbags.","info",{"met":508,"label":509,"note":510,"type":506},202.01,"TOUCHDOWN — INTO EAGLE CRATER","Bounced 26 times. Rolled into a 22-m crater by chance, surrounded by exposed bedrock.",{"met":512,"label":513,"note":514,"type":515},5452,"FINAL TRANSMISSION","2018-06-10. Planet-wide dust storm cuts solar power.","warning",{"met":517,"label":518,"note":519,"type":515},5700,"MISSION END","NASA declares end-of-mission 2019-02-13. 45.16 km traversed.","/orrery/images/missions/opportunity/06.webp"],"uses":{"params":["id"]}}]}
